spans.s:
andhakāla (m. or nt.),
(1) time of being blind: Kv 〔59.4〕, said of a son by his parents, (jarākāle yaṣṭibhūto) andhakāle mārgasyopadarśakaḥ (so read for text ˚opamardakaḥ; foll. by maraṇakāle piṇḍadātā);
(2) n. of a hell: Kv 〔18.14〕 (read Andhakāra? but this is not recorded as n. of a hell).
